      "writtenOn": "2025-03-19T21:59:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Discussed offline, but FTR another viable approach is to consider the SDM and SDC files artifacts that are covered by `ArtifactsPath` and hence reuse `OutputArtifacts` rather than adding these new types. That\u0027d also allow us to cut down some of the new `IArtd` methods in subsequent CLs.\n\nThe drawback is that it\u0027d mean adding another boolean flag in `ArtifactsPath` to specify whether the SDM/SDC files or the locally compiled artifacts are to be used. There\u0027s also little opportunity to reuse code in some places (i.e. the artd entry points would only mux on that flag), and `ArtifactPath`s with the flag set don\u0027t make sense in some functions like `dexopt`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 24,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "00b78c2ad4f44e11ffe5d588a01ec655c8a95616",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
